│     **What changed:**                                                                            │
│     - **New `fastapi/middleware/asyncexitstack.py`:** an `AsyncExitStackMiddleware` that creates │
│ an `AsyncExitStack` per request and stores it on `scope["fastapi_astack"]`.                      │
│     - **`fastapi/applications.py`:** overrides `build_middleware_stack` to place that middleware │
│ inside `ExceptionMiddleware`, so the stack unwinds after the response is sent.                   │
│     - **`fastapi/routing.py`:** the HTTP and WebSocket handlers now pass                         │
│ `scope["fastapi_astack"]` to `solve_dependencies` instead of opening their own `AsyncExitStack`. │
│                                                                                                  │
│     **Verification:**                                                                            │
│     - The modified modules compile and `import fastapi.applications` works.                      │
│     - `tests/test_dependency_contextmanager.py` has 20 passing tests and 2 failing ones          │
│ (`test_background_tasks` and `test_sync_background_tasks`). The failures show dependency exit    │
│ code now running after background tasks instead of before. That is the behaviour change the      │
│ issue asks for, but the old assertions still encode the previous order, so I did not update      │
│ them.                                                                                            │
│     - I did not run the `UploadFile` or `StreamingResponse` paths directly, and I did not check  │
│ the `UploadFile` cleanup timing against the issue.                                               │
│                                                                                                  │
│     The change is a single sentence: dependency exit code now runs on a request-scoped exit      │
│ stack that the middleware closes after the response is sent, instead of in a per-handler         │
│ `AsyncExitStack`.                                                                                │
